1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,700
So they're talking about something different in order

2
00:00:01,700 --> 00:00:04,760
to distract me, and that's really what I do have to assume.

3
00:00:04,760 --> 00:00:06,880
Let's see.

4
00:00:06,880 --> 00:00:09,360
So answer the question is good advice, and yes.

5
00:00:09,360 --> 00:00:10,940
And then also remember what I was saying

6
00:00:10,940 --> 00:00:14,480
about how it's important to distinguish between a question

7
00:00:14,480 --> 00:00:16,680
about a model from a question about the real world.

8
00:00:16,680 --> 00:00:20,180
So the question says, you know, in a Bertrand collusion model,

9
00:00:20,180 --> 00:00:22,280
is that a question about the model or about the real world?

10
00:00:22,880 --> 00:00:24,200
That's a question about the model.

11
00:00:24,200 --> 00:00:26,960
If there's a question that says, you know, does OPEC fit,

12
00:00:26,960 --> 00:00:29,900
does OPEC actually look like the Bertrand collusion model?

13
00:00:30,520 --> 00:00:31,440
What is that a question about?

14
00:00:32,120 --> 00:00:32,600
Real world.

15
00:00:32,600 --> 00:00:34,800
Then of course you need to know the model to answer the question,

16
00:00:35,200 --> 00:00:37,400
but it's not going to say, well, OPEC does,

17
00:00:37,400 --> 00:00:40,680
because what OPEC does is everybody in OPEC sets a price,

18
00:00:40,680 --> 00:00:42,560
and whoever sets the lowest price gets the entire

19
00:00:42,560 --> 00:00:45,560
world market, and that's not what actually happens

20
00:00:45,560 --> 00:00:46,560
with OPEC at all, is it?

21
00:00:47,300 --> 00:00:49,680
Right? As far as I've never heard about one country

22
00:00:49,680 --> 00:00:51,340
in the world selling all the oil for a year.

23
00:00:52,020 --> 00:00:53,720
As far as I know, that's never happened.

24
00:00:53,720 --> 00:00:58,020
So that would be a good point to say actually OPEC doesn't really

25
00:00:58,020 --> 00:01:00,540
fit the Bertrand collusion model well at all.

26
00:01:01,580 --> 00:01:04,380
Right? And then you could go and point out, the model says this,

27
00:01:04,580 --> 00:01:05,780
like here's what we see in the real world.

28
00:01:06,480 --> 00:01:08,180
So that would be a question about the real world.

29
00:01:08,460 --> 00:01:12,620
Again, normally I will try to be clear by saying something

30
00:01:12,620 --> 00:01:16,080
like in the real world, or other keywords that indicate

31
00:01:16,460 --> 00:01:17,880
that you need to be discussing facts.

32
00:01:18,700 --> 00:01:21,300
Right? You know, so now, you know,

33
00:01:21,300 --> 00:01:24,460
sometimes I'll ask questions along the lines of, you know,

34
00:01:24,600 --> 00:01:26,580
so does this model, like which,

35
00:01:26,580 --> 00:01:28,540
does this model adequately describe your behavior?

36
00:01:29,300 --> 00:01:32,680
Now, again, once in a while, someone will just say, yes,

37
00:01:32,680 --> 00:01:34,340
I always defect in a prisoner's lemma.

38
00:01:34,340 --> 00:01:39,000
So they're saying, hmm, I don't want to call them a liar,

39
00:01:39,000 --> 00:01:41,520
but if they don't say anything else, it doesn't seem

40
00:01:41,520 --> 00:01:42,720
like a very good answer still.

41
00:01:42,720 --> 00:01:44,520
So if the person would just say, look,

42
00:01:44,860 --> 00:01:47,380
people call me really weird and selfish and so on,

43
00:01:47,380 --> 00:01:49,740
but that's just how I am, and I don't care what people think

44
00:01:49,740 --> 00:01:51,300
about me, you know, it's a really good answer.

45
00:01:51,660 --> 00:01:51,980
All right?

46
00:01:51,980 --> 00:01:52,960
Then I believe you.

47
00:01:53,520 --> 00:01:55,960
But if you just give an answer where you say the model says

48
00:01:55,960 --> 00:01:57,880
this, and I do exactly that at the end.

49
00:01:58,440 --> 00:02:00,400
That's where it does, you know,

50
00:02:00,400 --> 00:02:03,620
where again it's possible that's true, but it's one

51
00:02:03,620 --> 00:02:05,940
where the explanation is not convincing,

52
00:02:05,940 --> 00:02:07,740
and so if you just flush it out more.

53
00:02:08,220 --> 00:02:10,980
Yeah, people call me a monster, but I always defect.

54
00:02:11,580 --> 00:02:12,400
All right?

55
00:02:12,400 --> 00:02:14,880
So that just adding that extra line is like, oh,

56
00:02:14,880 --> 00:02:16,420
it's pretty convincing.

57
00:02:16,420 --> 00:02:17,740
It shows that you're paying attention.

58
00:02:17,740 --> 00:02:21,660
So, yeah, so anyway, if there's questions

59
00:02:21,660 --> 00:02:23,640
about your own behavior and you're asked to explain it

60
00:02:24,020 --> 00:02:26,860
in general better if you can give a richer story, and,

61
00:02:26,860 --> 00:02:28,900
you know, a more observant story, right?

62
00:02:28,900 --> 00:02:30,280
You know, even if you are someone

63
00:02:30,280 --> 00:02:31,740
who fits the model very well, you can say, look,

64
00:02:31,740 --> 00:02:33,100
I realize that most people do this,

65
00:02:33,580 --> 00:02:34,500
but that's not what I do.

66
00:02:34,980 --> 00:02:35,740
I do something different.

67
00:02:35,740 --> 00:02:37,480
You know what I'm saying?

68
00:02:37,480 --> 00:02:39,620
So what I do is more, is constant with the model.

69
00:02:40,140 --> 00:02:42,500
Right? So, you know, you might say, look, I know most people,

70
00:02:42,780 --> 00:02:46,900
if they win a prize, go and blow it on some, you know,

71
00:02:46,900 --> 00:02:48,500
some temper on a big party or something,

72
00:02:48,500 --> 00:02:49,300
but that's not what I do.

73
00:02:49,380 --> 00:02:51,200
I go and raise my permanent income by 1%.

74
00:02:51,640 --> 00:02:54,140
That would be a good answer, because that would be my answer.

75
00:02:54,140 --> 00:02:56,740
So, of course, that's a good one.

76
00:02:57,420 --> 00:03:00,100
Yeah. So, anyway, so that's, anyway,

77
00:03:00,100 --> 00:03:01,520
so those are the main things to know.

78
00:03:02,040 --> 00:03:02,760
Let's see.

